# `az acr build ... .` uploads this whole folder to the registry. Its own
# default rules leave out only .git and .gitignore, so without this file every
# local file would go up too: a run store's output, the azd environment.
#
# This is an ALLOW-LIST. A deny-list must change each time the repository gets
# a new folder, and when it is not changed, nothing says so. The Dockerfiles
# copy six paths between them. Those six, and nothing else, go up.
#
# ONE FILE FOR BOTH BUILDS: `az acr build` reads the .dockerignore beside the
# build context, not beside the Dockerfile, so the engine image and the
# publish image share this list.
#
# tests/unit/BuildContext.Tests.ps1 reads each Dockerfile under docker/ and
# fails if one copies a path this file does not allow, or if this file allows
# a path no Dockerfile copies.
*

# the engine image (docker/Dockerfile)
!src/VmMigrationFactory
!src/guest
!docker/entrypoint.ps1

# the publish image (docker/publish/Dockerfile). It carries the service's
# code package, so it needs the two things the package is made of.
!src/facade/app
!src/facade/FacadeCore
!docker/publish/entrypoint.ps1
